# The install scripts have exactly ONE copy, in the product repository. This
# file makes rookery.sh serve them by redirecting to it, rather than vendoring
# copies here that would silently drift — the same failure the brand-logo
# manifest already has to be defended against.
#
# These MUST be real HTTP redirects, not Astro's `redirects:` config. That
# emits an HTML page carrying <meta http-equiv="refresh">, which a browser
# follows and `curl -fsSL` does not — so the advertised
# `curl -fsSL https://rookery.sh/install.sh | sh` would pipe an HTML document
# into a shell. curl and PowerShell's `irm` both follow a 302.
#
# The `!` suffix forces the rule ahead of static-file matching. Netlify and
# Cloudflare Pages both read this file; whichever host is chosen must honour it
# or express the same two rules in its own configuration.
#
# Both 404 until the product repository is public: raw.githubusercontent.com
# needs an authenticated request for a private repo. That is a release step, and
# no redirect can fix it.
/install.sh   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rookery-ai/rookery/main/install.sh   302!
/install.ps1  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rookery-ai/rookery/main/install.ps1  302!
